# McCore GUI System

## Key Classes

| Class | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `Gui<P extends CorePlayer>` | Interface for an inventory-backed GUI |
| `BaseGui<P>` | Abstract implementation; manages slots, click dispatch, listener lifecycle |
| `ClosableGui<P>` | `BaseGui` variant with a hook for when the last viewer closes |
| `PaginatedGui<P>` | `BaseGui` variant supporting multi-page inventory navigation |
| `GuiManager<P, CP>` | Manager that tracks which GUI each player currently has open |
| `Slot<P>` | A reusable inventory cell: holds an `ItemStack` and defines `onClick` behavior |
| `PlayerSettingSlot<P>` | Built-in slot for toggling a `PlayerSetting` |
| `NextPageSlot<P>` | Built-in slot for advancing a `PaginatedGui` |
| `PreviousPageSlot<P>` | Built-in slot for going back in a `PaginatedGui` |

## Checklist: Creating a New GUI

1. Subclass `BaseGui` (or `PaginatedGui` / `ClosableGui` as needed)
2. Pass `plugin`, `viewer`, title string, and inventory size to `super()`
3. Override `paintInventory()` — call `setSlot(index, slot)` for each cell
4. Create `Slot` implementations for each interactive cell (see below)
5. Open for a player via `GuiManager.trackPlayerGui()` then `player.openInventory(gui.getInventory())`

## Minimal BaseGui Template

```java
public class MyGui extends BaseGui<MyPlayer> {

    public MyGui(@NotNull MyPlugin plugin, @NotNull MyPlayer viewer) {
        super(plugin, viewer, "My GUI Title", 54); // 54 slots = 6 rows
    }

    @Override
    public void paintInventory() {
        setSlot(0, new MyActionSlot());
        setSlot(8, new PlayerSettingSlot<>(getViewer(), MySetting.MY_SETTING_KEY));
        // Unset slots use the default empty slot — no need to fill manually
    }
}
```

## Implementing a Slot

Slots are typically anonymous classes or static inner classes, not separate files, unless shared across GUIs.

```java
public class MyActionSlot extends Slot<MyPlayer> {

    public MyActionSlot() {
        super(new ItemBuilder(Material.DIAMOND).setName("<aqua>Click Me").build());
    }

    @Override
    public boolean onClick(@NotNull MyPlayer viewer, @NotNull ClickType clickType) {
        // Perform action
        viewer.getAsBukkitPlayer().ifPresent(p -> p.sendMessage("Clicked!"));
        return true; // true = cancel the underlying InventoryClickEvent
    }
}
```

## Listener Lifecycle (Automatic)

`BaseGui` implements `Listener`. It **self-registers** with the Bukkit plugin manager when the first player opens it and **self-deregisters** when the last player closes it. Do not manually register or unregister GUI instances.

## Opening and Tracking

```java
GuiManager<MyPlayer, MyPlugin> guiManager = plugin.registryAccess()
    .registry(RegistryKey.MANAGER)
    .manager(CoreManagerKey.CORE_GUI_MANAGER);

MyGui gui = new MyGui(plugin, corePlayer);
guiManager.trackPlayerGui(corePlayer, gui);
gui.paintInventory();
corePlayer.getAsBukkitPlayer().ifPresent(p -> p.openInventory(gui.getInventory()));
```

## Closing and Cleanup

```java
// Stop tracking when a player's GUI is closed programmatically
guiManager.stopTrackingPlayer(corePlayer);

// Check and retrieve the open GUI
Optional<Gui<MyPlayer>> openGui = guiManager.getOpenedGui(corePlayer);
```

## Refreshing a GUI

To update a GUI that one or more players are currently viewing:

```java
// Repaint all inventories for every player viewing this GUI instance
guiManager.refreshGui(gui);
```

This fires a `GuiRefreshEvent` and re-calls `paintInventory()` across all open views.

## PaginatedGui

```java
public class MyPaginatedGui extends PaginatedGui<MyPlayer> {

    private final List<MyItem> items;

    public MyPaginatedGui(@NotNull MyPlugin plugin, @NotNull MyPlayer viewer, @NotNull List<MyItem> items) {
        super(plugin, viewer, "My Paged GUI", 54);
        this.items = items;
    }

    @Override
    public int getMaximumPage() {
        return Math.max(1, (int) Math.ceil(items.size() / (double) CONTENT_SLOTS_PER_PAGE));
    }

    @Override
    public void paintInventoryForPage(@NotNull Inventory inventory, int page) {
        // Place NextPageSlot / PreviousPageSlot at fixed positions
        setSlot(inventory, 53, new NextPageSlot<>(this));
        setSlot(inventory, 45, new PreviousPageSlot<>(this));

        // Populate content slots for the current page
        int start = (page - 1) * CONTENT_SLOTS_PER_PAGE;
        for (int i = start; i < Math.min(start + CONTENT_SLOTS_PER_PAGE, items.size()); i++) {
            int slotIndex = i - start;
            setSlot(inventory, slotIndex, new MyItemSlot(items.get(i)));
        }
    }
}
```

## PlayerSettingSlot

Renders a toggle-able `PlayerSetting`. The slot automatically reflects the current value and updates it on click.

```java
// In paintInventory():
setSlot(22, new PlayerSettingSlot<>(getViewer(), MySetting.MY_SETTING_KEY));
```

`PlayerSetting` must be registered in `PlayerSettingRegistry` during bootstrap for persistence to work.

